userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: Archimedes' spiral r = θ is the polar curve whose radius grows in direct proportion to the swept angle, so every plotted point has coordinates of the form (θ, θ) and each full turn widens the loop by the same amount.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): In r = θ the two numbers in every polar coordinate are identical — the angle swept so far IS the distance from the origin, which is why the loop widens evenly with each turn.
DEMO STEPS: 3 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

